  "worked_solution": "Speed is a special unit rate applied to moving objects. It is defined as *the distance traveled per unit of time*:\n\n$$\n\\text{speed}=\\frac{\\text{distance}}{\\text{time}}\n$$\n\nTo find the speed in meters per minute, we divide the number of meters, $960,$ by the number of minutes, $16.$ This gives,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{960}{16} & =\\frac{960÷8}{16÷8} \\\\  & =\\frac{120}{2} \\\\  & =120÷2 \\\\  & =60.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, Mary's speed was $60$ meters per minute.",
